<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Haupaix et al. (2018) & Inaba et al. (2019) somite-prepatterned Agouti signaling and melanocyte gap-junction reaction-diffusion in galliform plumage stripes (Galliform chicks — Japanese quail (Coturnix japonica), common pheasant (Phasianus colchicus), guineafowl (Numida meleagris), partridge (Alectoris rufa), and turkey (Meleagris gallopavo))",
        "Haupaix et al. (2018) & Inaba et al. (2019) somite-prepatterned Agouti signaling and melanocyte gap-junction reaction-diffusion in galliform plumage stripes faithfully reproduces Galliform chicks — Japanese quail (Coturnix japonica), common pheasant (Phasianus colchicus), guineafowl (Numida meleagris), partridge (Alectoris rufa), and turkey (Meleagris gallopavo) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Galliform chicks — Japanese quail (Coturnix japonica), common pheasant (Phasianus colchicus), guineafowl (Numida meleagris), partridge (Alectoris rufa), and turkey (Meleagris gallopavo) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 46.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-audit) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py> ;
    schema:about "Galliform chicks — Japanese quail (Coturnix japonica), common pheasant (Phasianus colchicus), guineafowl (Numida meleagris), partridge (Alectoris rufa), and turkey (Meleagris gallopavo)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py; output: docs/media/avian_plumage_somite_stripes_comparison.png; organism: Galliform chicks — Japanese quail (Coturnix japonica), common pheasant (Phasianus colchicus), guineafowl (Numida meleagris), partridge (Alectoris rufa), and turkey (Meleagris gallopavo); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 02a8479af5560c95d12d26c94859ee0f020f922c46969b9a4243ec2f1ee4dce8; artifact_sha256: 02e43fa9a09c165fdbe30288a07b86756d896b7509ec5647f9471be53a60ab00; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/avian_plumage_somite_stripes_reference.json=6029de05099340f7..., datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/galliform_chick_stripes_specimen.jpg=78337aba30f62614..., datasets/avian_plumage_somite_stripes/scout_manifest.json=acb7ac44b807e24b...}" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1230374>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aar4777>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaw1969>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
